      "content": "The memo should frame leadership not as an arbiter of political correctness, but as a neutral facilitator focused on ensuring that all voices are heard before reaching conclusions, regardless of alignment with corporate culture. It must explicitly commit to reviewing the context of any removal, emphasizing that actions are taken only when they materially disrupt workflows or create a hostile atmosphere, rather than suppressing ideas. By grounding decisions in observable behavior and impact on team morale rather than political stance, the policy avoids appearing to favor a specific ideology while still protecting the company's functional integrity. This approach shifts the narrative from \"we ban you\" to \"we ensure everyone can participate without the conversation derailing our shared goals,\" which encourages dialogue within safe limits.",
